--
libstdc++ 13 <filesystem>: the bodies of _Sp_counted_ptr::_M_dispose
(bits/shared_ptr_base.h:427) and the __shared_count(_Ptr) constructor (913)
are dropped: they are instantiated with a non-pointer _Ptr ("delete takes
a pointer type operand, but got 'signed int'", also strong_ordering and
partial_ordering) while overload resolution for path's constructors
considers __shared_count(_Ptr).  Being reduced.  With the libstdc++ 16
headers the front end crashes instead (SIGSEGV), the root cause being
cpp11_partial_specialization_const_T_matching_const_array
(incrementable_traits<const char[2]>).  g++ 13 accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
